   "fix": "Name the step with the existing lemma: `have h := (PerfectField.separable_iff_squarefree.mpr hp).eval\u2082_derivative_ne_zero (RingHom.id K) (by rwa [eval\u2082_id]); rwa [eval\u2082_id] at h` (or `simpa`/`simpa using` on both sides).",
   "issue": "`(PerfectField.separable_iff_squarefree.mpr hp).eval\u2082_derivative_ne_zero (RingHom.id K) hx` type-checks only through the wrapper defeq `Polynomial.eval = eval\u2082 (RingHom.id _)`: `hx : p.eval x = 0` is passed where `p.eval\u2082 (RingHom.id K) x = 0` is expected, and the result `(derivative p).eval\u2082 (RingHom.id K) x \u2260 0` is accepted for `p.derivative.eval x \u2260 0`. Nothing in the proof documents this; it depends on `Polynomial.eval` staying a transparent def (its callee `eval\u2082` is already `irreducible_def` upstream, so this reducibility is not stable).",
